Work around GCC 11 limitations in stdexec sender declarations.

Copyright (c) 2026 Pratyksh Gupta

Current stdexec uses deduction guides for class templates nested in sender
customization point types. GCC 11 rejects those guides because it requires them
at namespace scope. Spell the sender template arguments explicitly instead;
this preserves the deduced, decayed types without relying on the unsupported
syntax.

GCC 11 also performs the non-dependent lookup of __nothrow_transform before it
reaches that member's declaration in __sequence_t. Move the private helpers
before their first use without changing their implementation.

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSL-1.0

